CVE-2026-124286.workaround:
Restrict TLS client connections to TLS 1.3 by setting versions to ['tlsv1.3'] in the client's ssl options.

If a client must use TLS 1.2, offer only the static RSA key exchange cipher suites. These suites have no ServerKeyExchange message. They provide no forward secrecy, and many servers do not accept them.

RsaOnly = ssl:filter_cipher_suites(
    ssl:cipher_suites(all, 'tlsv1.2'),
    [{key_exchange, fun(rsa) -> true; (_) -> false end}]
),
Opts = [
    {verify, verify_peer},
    {cacerts, public_key:cacerts_get()},
    {versions, ['tlsv1.2']},
    {ciphers, RsaOnly},
    {server_name_indication, "www.example.com"},
    {customize_hostname_check, [
        {match_fun, public_key:pkix_verify_hostname_match_fun(https)}
    ]}
].
